# Triaged hits from scripts/audit-silent-reverts.sh — one `<sha> <reason>` per
# line. A commit listed here is a content rollback we have LOOKED AT and
# accepted. Anything not listed fails the audit; clearing it means writing the
# reason down, not deleting the line.
#
# Format: 7-char sha, whitespace, one-line reason.

dcca7b5 THE INCIDENT (rangerhq-8rtf). Silently reverted ef8d35f, a landed P1 fix, for 3h52m15s with its regression pin re-skipped. Cause: ef8d35f was committed from a private GIT_INDEX_FILE, leaving the shared .git/index holding pre-fix blobs; this bd sync committed them back. Re-landed byte-identical by 1cc432e. Left on main deliberately - rewriting history is the operator's call.
1cc432e The REPAIR of dcca7b5, not a defect. Re-lands ef8d35f's diff byte-identical, so it reads as a rollback of dcca7b5 and is flagged by construction. Its own message shows the author believed this was uncommitted leftover work rather than a revert - which is the evidence that nobody knew.
21653f9 Benign, pre-crew. The documented herdr-native architecture pivot (35 files, -4387 lines, tmux implementation moved to the tmux-reference branch). examples/config.yaml returns to an older shape because slot_preference was removed - herdr owns layout now. Single author, deliberate, described in the commit message.
9daf91f Benign, and the deletion IS the point of the commit. `.beads/interactions.jsonl` (a bd runtime log) was deliberately untracked so activity stops accumulating into a public repo; the same commit adds it to .gitignore and writes the privacy model into NOTES.md. Verified: still gitignored (.gitignore:4), still absent from HEAD. Flagged only because the deletion rule (rangerhq-ypn1) cannot know a removal was the intent.
631bda7 Benign. The rhq -> posse command rename (rangerhq-tyay). Four of its deletions are renames that also EDIT the file, so they are not exact-blob moves and the move exception does not cover them; `git show -M` names all four as renames and cmd/posse/{cockpit_test.go,gateschain_qa_test.go,main.go,main_test.go} exist at HEAD. Nothing was lost, the content moved one directory over.
e82338c Benign, and the same class as 631bda7. The clean room gains fedora/rhel/arch (ranger-base-5cj4), and its debian image is the old file renamed: `git show --numstat -M e82338c` names etc/cleanroom/{Dockerfile => Dockerfile.debian}, +38/-10 — a rename that also EDITS, so it is not an exact-blob move and the move exception cannot see it. Nothing was lost: all four of etc/cleanroom/Dockerfile.{arch,debian,fedora,rhel} are at HEAD. Second rename+edit in this file; a third one means fixing the move exception to ask git for rename similarity instead of exact blob identity.
2eae58a Benign, and the THIRD rename+edit in this file after 631bda7 and e82338c. ADR 0012 D2 took the crew brand out of the nine seeded PIDs (rangerhq-o7y4), and the filename IS the persona name, so examples/agents/ranger.md became examples/agents/ops.md: `git show --numstat -M 2eae58a` names examples/agents/{ranger.md => ops.md}, +2/-2, similarity index 97% — a rename that also EDITS, so it is not an exact-blob move and the move exception cannot see it. Nothing was lost: HEAD still carries nine PIDs under examples/agents/ with ops.md among them, and ranger.md is absent by construction. The third strike e82338c's line called: fixing the move exception to ask git for rename similarity instead of exact blob identity is filed as ranger-base-en75, deliberately not inside this P1 release unblock (ranger-base-ae6k) — a detector change whose failure direction is a false NEGATIVE gets its own verification pass.
